<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>JETCARP third-party licences</title>
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 60rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: rgba(127, 127, 127, 0.12); padding: 0.8rem; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  h2 { margin-top: 2.5rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(127, 127, 127, 0.4); padding-top: 1rem; }
  ul.crates { columns: 2; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .overview li { margin: 0.1rem 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party licences</h1>
<p>JETCARP's own code is under the Unlicense or the MIT licence, at your option (see
<code>COPYING</code>, <code>UNLICENSE</code> and <code>LICENSE-MIT</code>). Files in JETCARP derived
from other people's work are listed in <code>THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</code>.</p>
<p>This page lists the Rust libraries that JETCARP's release builds contain, for Linux, Windows and
macOS together, and the licence under which each is used. Where a library offers a choice of
licences, the one shown is the one JETCARP uses. It was generated by
<a href="https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-about">cargo-about</a> from the crates' own licence
files.</p>

<h2>C libraries built into the program</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>SQLite</strong> (through <code>libsqlite3-sys</code>), which is in the public domain:
  "The author disclaims copyright to this source code. In place of a legal notice, here is a
  blessing: May you do good and not evil. May you find forgiveness for yourself and forgive others.
  May you share freely, never taking more than you give."</li>
  <li><strong>Zstandard</strong> (through <code>zstd-sys</code>), used under the BSD licence that
  appears below with the <code>zstd-sys</code> crate.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Overview</h2>
<ul class="overview">
{{#each overview}}
  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>

{{#each licenses}}
<h2 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h2>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul class="crates">
{{#each used_by}}
  <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
